public static int indexOfLastSeparator(String filename) {
    // Edge case: If the filename is null, return -1
    if (filename == null) {
        return -1;
    }

    // Get the length of the filename for iteration
    int len = filename.length();

    // Iterate from the end to find the last separator
    for (int i = len - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        // Check if the current character is a separator (Unix: '/' and Windows: '\\')
        if (filename.charAt(i) == '/' || filename.charAt(i) == '\\') {
            return i; // Return the position of the separator
        }
    }

    // If no separator is found, return -1
    return -1;
}
```

Please note that this method assumes the filename is in either Unix or Windows format. It checks for both forward (`/`) and backward (`\`) slashes and returns the first occurring one. This might not be the case in some filenames.

